id: pm-context-sdk-codecs-utf8
title: Adopt SDK codecs and UTF-8 context receipt accounting
description: "Implement G5 from the 2026-11-06 adoption audit: public SDK codecs and UTF-8 output token accounting, retaining domain selection, byte limits and indivisible evidence."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[2]: output,sdk-adoption
created_at: "2026-11-06T12:10:29.064Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T12:28:04.160Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: Real non-Git tracker tests; complete serialized UTF-8 accounting; SDK codec round trips; preserved omissions and exact citations; behavioral revert proofs.
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T12:10:36.280Z",codex-sol,"Read companion pm-cli-website-nzm7 (G5) and its audit acceptance criteria without modifying the companion. Replace local character estimates and handwritten TOON grammar with installed public SDK APIs; keep byte budgets, domain ranking, completeness, restoration and indivisible witnesses. Main baseline 87b6e4f; pinned SDK 2026.11.4 retained. Public registry currently reports CLI 2026.11.6; audit target is 2026.11.5."
  "2026-11-06T12:15:19.384Z",codex-sol,"Implemented SDK estimatePmOutputTokens over UTF-8 bytes for facts, receipt overhead and projection ranking. JSON protocol overhead stabilizes including its final digits/newline. Handwritten TOON containers now use public host encodeToon (sdk/testing is the pinned host generic codec export); next-evidence retains encodePmTableRows and its complete encoding metadata. Freshness/evidence sizing stays in bytes, with SDK-encoded row costs. Existing direct TOON consumers also use the host codec. No whole-envelope estimated-token fitter exists here: context selection already delegates to packContextCandidates; since explicitly budgets utf8-bytes, so converting either byte contract to estimated tokens would violate G5."
  "2026-11-06T12:17:15.232Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral reverts verified in a disposable source copy, restoring only one changed function at a time from baseline 87b6e4f. serveContextReceipt: 2 assertion failures; estimateTokens, encodeNextEvidencePlan, encodeWitnessReport, encodeFreshness, encodeEvidencePack: 1 assertion failure each. No import/build failures. Restoring all candidate functions passed 7/7. Targeted SDK tests passed 7/7 and pm test execution passed. Existing focused suites found one presentation-only expectation for quoted TOON FRESH; replaced it with host-codec semantic decoding."
  "2026-11-06T12:19:47.741Z",codex-sol,"The published 2026.10.23 sdk/testing declarations also export encodeToon/decodeToon, so the existing peer floor supports the codec adoption and no dependency bump is needed. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring gate pass; no separate lint script is declared. git diff --check passes. Strict tracker health with required merge drivers passes. Full npm and isolated-identity Bun release gates will be recorded before final tracker release and changelog regeneration."
  "2026-11-06T12:22:15.327Z",codex-sol,"Local validation: seven new SDK regressions pass; six isolated behavioral-revert variants produce seven expected assertion failures, restored candidate passes 7/7; pm test execution passes. Existing focused suites passed 53/54, with the sole quoted-TOON presentation assertion corrected and its CLI scenario rerun separately. Typecheck, test compilation, docstrings, whitespace and strict tracker health pass. Per the task gate split, full npm/Bun release and coverage gates run in CI; the local exploratory full gate was stopped during existing long model suites without a failure verdict. Review will use the required queue and final-head CI results."
  "2026-11-06T12:27:32.539Z",codex-sol,"Self-review found a TOON byte-admission edge: the host encodes an empty array inline, while populated arrays have counted headers. Repeated single-row deltas can undercount the format transition and refuse near-boundary packets that should admit a shorter prefix. Add full-size minus one/exact/plus one byte regressions, derive the empty-to-populated overhead from SDK single/double renders, and retain linear work and the final complete-output byte guard."
  "2026-11-06T12:28:02.329Z",codex-sol,"Correction to the self-review hypothesis: the new minus-one/exact/plus-one byte regression passes on the pushed implementation. Measuring SDK empty/single/double encodings shows zero empty-to-populated overhead after row bytes are subtracted; empty and populated headers have equal UTF-8 size for a one-digit count. No production sizing defect was reproduced and no algorithm change is needed. Retain the stronger exact-boundary regression as additional evidence; the earlier six behavioral revert proofs remain valid."
